{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringConeIcosahedral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringConeIcosahedral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BringCone"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_unitJ_flips_chiralGamma_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_unitJ_flips_chiralGamma_i","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L101-L106","doc":"The instance `w = j`, `u = i`: the half-turn about `j` flips `Γ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_flips_chiralGammaU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_flips_chiralGammaU","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L93-L99","doc":"**…and so the symmetry `L_w` swaps the two chiralities**: it carries `Γ_u` to\n`−Γ_u = Γ_{−u}`. A group containing such a `w` identifies L with R at `u`; it cannot\nfix a handedness there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.conjBy_neg_of_anticomm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.conjBy_neg_of_anticomm","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L83-L91","doc":"**A perpendicular half-turn sends `u` to `−u`.** If `w` anticommutes with `u` and\n`normSq w = 1`, then `w u w̄ = −u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.conjBy_unitI_unitJ_fixed_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.conjBy_unitI_unitJ_fixed_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L67-L81","doc":"**No common fixed admissible unit.** If `2` is cancellable in `R`, a pure quaternion\nfixed by conjugation by both `i` and `j` is zero. (Conjugation by `i` is the half-turn\nabout the `i`-axis, by `j` the half-turn about the `j`-axis; their fixed lines meet only\nat `0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.normSq_conjBy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.normSq_conjBy","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L61-L65","doc":"Conjugation scales the norm by `normSq g ^ 2`; a unit `g` preserves it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.re_conjBy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.re_conjBy","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L54-L59","doc":"Conjugation scales the real part by `normSq g`; in particular it preserves \"pure\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_conj_chiralGammaU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_conj_chiralGammaU","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L47-L52","doc":"**A left-multiplication symmetry acts on the chirality unit by conjugation.**\n`L_g ∘ Γ_u ∘ L_{ḡ} = Γ_{g u ḡ}`, for every `g` (no norm condition: `L_{ḡ}` is written\nexplicitly, and is the inverse of `L_g` when `normSq g = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.conjBy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.conjBy","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeIcosahedral.lean#L44-L45","doc":"Conjugation of an admissible unit by `g`: `u ↦ g u ḡ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}